      "committer": {
        "name": "sn3ro",
        "email": "zak.darek@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T21:20:37Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): a semi-transparent viewport_hover veils the facet in its own colour\n\nReview of #3993: the facet veil read viewport_hover's r(), g() and b(),\nwhich Color32 stores multiplied by alpha, and multiplied them again.\nA theme's #FF000080 gave a [45, 0, 0, 90] veil, not [90, 0, 0, 90].\nground_ink::facet_veil reads the colour unmultiplied first. The opaque\nbuilt-in gold gives the same veil as before.\n\nPinned by viewport_inks::the_facet_veil_keeps_the_hover_colour_of_a_semi_transparent_token.\n\nRefs #1120\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
